t-fifty-years-mcgeorge-bundy.jpg","pageCount":756,"readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0.074,"accessibilityScore":0.195,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"popular","score":0.34,"confidence":"low","evidence":["trade publisher signal: Random House / Penguin Random House","major-award recognition"]},{"id":"synthesis","score":0.2,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"from\"","catalog text contains \"history of\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"Nuclear threats and atomic weapons function as effective diplomatic bargaining chips that have repeatedly helped resolve or defuse dangerous crises and shape key Cold War outcomes.","confidence":0.72},"academicOrientation":{"score":45,"confidence":0.55},"profileConfidence":0.8,"model":"gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"84ab002bd2b054b2babb3b3fc417bcf85f6750bd596c78a041598d1a3f73e7af","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"primarySubject":"Politics & Government","secondarySubjects":["War & Military","History"],"confidence":"high","rationale":"The book primarily examines nuclear weapons as tools of diplomatic policy and statecraft, making Politics & Government the most fitting primary subject, with War & Military and History as relevant secondary subjects.","method":"llm","model":"gpt-4o-mini","reviewStatus":"generated","inputHash":"f31e3b6819dc2f947e2b9cddac5167429c842ff73198dd3629cd3c39beb608e0","summary":"An informed and informative appreciation of nuclear weapons as instruments of diplomatic policy. A special assistant for national security affairs in both the JFK and LBJ administrations who now teaches at NYU, Bundy provides a detailed history of the vital role played by atomic arms in geopolitics since the 1938 discovery of fission. At the outset, he reviews the factors that allowed the US--but not allies or enemies--to develop A-bombs for use in WW II and the causes of its subsequent commitment to thermonuclear weapons during the early stages of the Cold War. Leaving little doubt that the bomb was an important bargaining chip in the negotiations that ended hostilities in Korea and removed Soviet missiles from Cuba, the author examines other instances in which the implicit threat of nuclear action has helped resolve or defuse potentially dangerous crises. Cases in point include 1969 clashes along the Sino-Soviet frontier, the Yom Kippur War, and America's protracted involvement in Vietnam. In addition to a chronological narrative that brings the fearful story of atomic arms and statecraft into the current era's demanding stalemate, Bundy offers thoughtful appraisals of what it means to the British, Chinese, French, Israelis, and USSR as well as the US to be nuclear powers in an aerospace age.","subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Politics and government","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-danger-and-survival-choices-about-the-bomb-in-the-first-fifty-years-mcgeorge-bundy"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Foreign relations","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-danger-and-survival-choices-about-the-bomb-in-the-first-fifty-years-mcgeorge-bundy"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"United States","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-danger-and-survival-choices-about-the-bomb-in-the-first-fifty-years-mcgeorge-bundy"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"History","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-danger-and-survival-choices-about-the-bomb-in-the-first-fifty-years-mcgeorge-bundy"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Arms race","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-danger-and-survival-choices-about-the-bomb-in-the-first-fifty-years-mcgeorge-bundy"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject